00:00:39.979 --> 00:00:46.979
Traveling back in time, Ted Grant origin story.
He debuted in 1942 as a professional boxer.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:52.190
He grew up super poor but his father taught
him to be an animal of sorts in the ring.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:55.659
To earn extra money to survive he got a job
on the loading docks.

00:00:55.659 --> 00:00:58.789
One night he sees a couple thugs ambushing
someone, he beats the shit out of said thugs

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:02.089
and the person he saved turns out to be a
washed up prize fighter. That person then

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:03.319
backs Ted in an official capacity as a boxing
heavyweight contender. Thus begins his pro

00:01:03.319 --> 00:01:04.600
boxing career.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:11.600
That’s where he got his name Wildcat, for
being so vicious in the ring. He was really

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:13.909
big, really tough and really fast.

00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:18.170
Eventually a local mobster fixed one of his
matches and then framed Ted for it. After

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.070
he cleared his name he took up the name Wildcat
as a superhero alias and started fighting

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.039
crime.

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:28.560
He had been inspired by the original green
lantern, Alan Scott. As a DC Character he

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:35.560
spent most of his time jumping around titles
but his longest runs were in Justice Society.

00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:41.100
He does have some strange mystical powers.
The Dark Lord Mordu said that Wildcat has

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:46.229
9 lives, like he can die and come back 9 times.
And as long as all those deaths don’t happen

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:50.659
too close together, the lives will refresh
and he’ll always have nine lives.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:54.479
On the show it’s more likely that Arrow
will just show him as being crazy resilient,

00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:57.140
like Mirakuru levels of toughness.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:01.289
Geoff Johns made him one of the central Justice
Society characters when he started writing

00:02:01.289 --> 00:02:05.829
that book back in the early 2000s. That was
actually one of his first big comic runs,

00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:09.170
it was before he brought back Barry Allen
in Flash Rebirth. So you could also think

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:14.030
of JSA as being a Geoff Johns origin story,
at least at DC Comics.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:19.730
By that time in the comics they changed Ted
Grant’s backstory and just made him a retired

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:22.970
heavyweight champ turned superhero who trained
all the big Justice Society an Justice League

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.160
characters how to fight.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.960
He did have a son that he never knew about
until he was a teenager. His name was Tommy

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.650
Bronson, and in a twist on the Wildcat legacy,
the son is a werecat who can transform. So

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:37.090
son of Wildcat is a real life cat. That was
a big Vandal Savage arc in case you guys ever

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.830
want to read it. Just read Geoff Johns run
on JSA, it was really cool.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:44.640
JR Ramirez, the actor they cast looks about
old enough to be a retired pro boxer, so they

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.830
might just go with a modified origin story
on the tv show. They posted pictures from

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:52.090
the set of Oliver in a boxing ring, so either
Oliver will meet Ted Grant during his final

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:56.090
fight or he’ll already be retired and just
be a boxing trainer.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:03:00.630
Either way, I think the most exciting thing
to look forward to is Wildcat teaching Oliver

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:05.040
how to be a better fighter. That’s Wildcat’s
biggest thing, being the guy who taught all

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.570
the major A-List superheroes how to fight.
Or at least the ones who weren’t aliens.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:15.570
Superman doesn’t need to be a nimble fighter.
He’s indestructible and he has super speed.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:20.000
Batman vs Wildcat was another really fun comic
book arc though.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.100
I do think Arrow will age him down a little,
in the comics he comes off a little like an

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:28.760
Old Man, or at least he thinks of himself
as being way past his prime. His JSA team

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:33.500
was Alan Scott, Jay Garrick, a lot of the
classic golden age heroes. When Geoff Johns

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.040
took over the comic, part of the plot was
them re-forming the team.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.790
Like they had been retired as superheroes
for a while.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:46.160
If you remember, Hawkman was another one of
the bigger Justice Society characters. Michael

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.190
Shanks from Stargate played him on Smallville.
But there were a bunch of other characters

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:55.230
that Arrow could tease this season and then
bring on in the future.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:59.740
Doctor Fate was a big team member of Wildcats
too, they teased him in the Constantine Pilot.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:03.310
You just see the helmet of Fate. Smallville
also did Doctor Fate too during their Justice

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:03.520
Society Arc.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.700
I think Arrow will do more of a Justice Society
of Arrow as in JS Arrow. I don’t think they

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:06.430
